WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.800
In this video, you enable the monitoring add-on in SUSE Virtualization, then view the metrics that it collects for a running virtual machine.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:15.950
Add-ons, under Advanced, lists optional components. The rancher-monitoring add-on is disabled.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.780
Open its actions menu.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:27.900
Select Enable. SUSE Virtualization deploys Prometheus, Grafana, and Alertmanager into the cluster.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:34.150
After a few minutes, the add-on state changes to Deploy Successful.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.290
Next, open Virtual Machines.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.540
Select the running virtual machine demo-metrics.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:48.480
A new Virtual Machine Metrics tab is now available. Select it.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:59.730
Grafana panels show this virtual machine's CPU and memory usage, and its storage traffic, latency, and IOPS.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:05.150
The cluster dashboard also gains metrics. Open Dashboard.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:10.970
Below the capacity summary, select Cluster Metrics.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:18.200
Cluster Metrics charts CPU utilization, load average, and memory utilization of the hosts.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:25.580
Virtual Machine Metrics compares resource usage across virtual machines.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:33.250
The charts show CPU, memory, and storage usage for up to ten virtual machines.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:40.258
Monitoring is enabled and the virtual machine reports its metrics. Next, you balance virtual machines automatically.
